& [ResidualRisk]
  + component metadata and canonical containment checks do not provide a hostile concurrent-filesystem transaction lock
  + safe standard-library rename and parent-directory flush behavior remains platform dependent and must be empirically gated
  + a post-replacement validation or durability failure requires later recovery-owned rollback execution
  + synthetic fixture evidence does not prove a real activation policy recovery owner semantic quality or operator consent

& [Decision]
  + the residual risks are acceptable only for explicit quiescent disposable fixtures
  + any unsupported platform durability behavior produces a refusal rather than a weakened success claim
